        "AbstractText": "Polycystic ovary syndrome is the most common endocrinopathy recognized in women of childbearing age with a prevalence of 4-12%. The prevalence of the disorder in adolescent population is poorly defined. The pathogenesis as well as the management of this disorder is widely debated."
